dialogue bramwick
  node root bramwick "Fenn. It's past the night bell. If you're here to work, I admire it. If you're here to ask for something, I don't."
    > "I want to sign on with the Marrow." if not has licence -> berth
    > "I have my licence, sir." if has licence -> licence
    > "Just finishing the ledgers, sir." -> loiter
    > "Goodnight, sir." -> bye
  node loiter bramwick "Good man. The ledger is never finished, Fenn. That is what I love about it."
    > "Actually, sir, about the Marrow…" if not has licence -> berth
    > "Goodnight, sir." -> bye
  node berth bramwick "The Marrow, for the Straits. Every hand who sails from Vela carries a Seafarer's Licence, with the harbour stamp on it."
    -> berth2
  node berth2 bramwick "Pirates included. Pirates especially. We are a well-run port."
    -> form
  node form bramwick "I cannot stamp anything after the night bell. Regulation fourteen."
    -> form2
  node form2 bramwick "However, any clerk of this house may stamp in the Harbourmaster's absence. And after the bell, Fenn, I am, legally, absent."
    > "So I could stamp it myself?" -> self
    > "Where is the stamp?" -> key
      set knows_key
      note stamp_drawer "The licence needs the harbour stamp. It lives in Bramwick's desk drawer, and he lost the key to Marta at cards."
    > "Is there a berth left?" -> claim
  node self bramwick "I said no such thing. I recited several regulations, loudly. The forms are on my desk. The stamp is in my drawer."
    > "And the drawer is…?" -> key
      set knows_key
  node key bramwick "Locked. The key is with Marta at the Salty Keel. I lost it to her at cards. A man of my standing does not discuss it further."
    > "Is there a berth left?" -> claim
    > "Right. Marta." -> bye
  node claim bramwick "One. Claimed and paid for by Mr Cray's office. A claim stands, Fenn, unless the claimant has defrauded this harbour. Mr Cray is a very respectable man."
    > "That sounded like a hint, sir." -> hint
    > "Why are you helping me?" -> care
  node hint bramwick "It was a regulation. I am full of them tonight. Get your licence first. Then we'll see what else you can find."
    > "Where is the stamp?" if not knows_key -> key
      set knows_key
    > "Goodnight, sir." -> bye
  node care bramwick "Three years you've kept my day-books without a blot. Your father sailed for the Straits, and I won't be the man who kept his son ashore."
    -> care2
  node care2 bramwick "I have been enough of a man like that already."
    > "Where is the stamp?" if not knows_key -> key
      set knows_key
    > "Thank you, sir. I'll try to blot something, for old times' sake." -> bye
  node licence bramwick "Do you. I can't stamp it, Fenn, but I can certainly read it. Hand it over."
    > "Here it is. And the Arcadia's manifest." if ledger_read and has manifest and not met_rook -> confess
    > "Here it is. And the Arcadia's manifest." if ledger_read and has manifest and met_rook -> confess_rook
    > "Here it is." if (not ledger_read or not has manifest) -> deferred
    > "On second thoughts, sir, it needs another read." -> bye
  node deferred bramwick "A fine licence. The berth is still Mr Cray's. Bring me the Arcadia's manifest copy; the chandler keeps one of every ship he provisions."
    -> deferred2
  node deferred2 bramwick "And read the harbour ledger yourself, Fenn. Don't let me read it to you."
    > "Yes, sir. I'll read it myself. In good light. Twice." -> bye
  node confess fenn "The Arcadia: lost three days before she was late, in your hand. Quarantine dues, paid by Cray & Co. And a navigator 'discharged at sea'. By whom, sir, in the middle of the sea?"
    -> confess2
  node confess_rook fenn "The Arcadia: lost three days before she was late, in your hand. Quarantine dues, paid by Cray & Co. And a navigator 'discharged at sea', now drinking in the Salty Keel."
    -> confess2
  node confess2 bramwick "I was paid. I told myself it was a kindness: a quick line in the book instead of a long wait at the window. It was not a kindness. It was three hundred crowns."
    -> confess3
  node confess3 bramwick "Mr Cray's claim is void, regulation two, and you're on the Marrow. I wrote your father down, Fenn. I never once saw him go under. Don't make me write you down as lost."
    > "I won't, sir." -> END
      act 1
    > "You wrote him down, sir. Three days early." -> early
    > "You told me to read it. Thank you for that." -> thanked
  node early bramwick "I did. I have read that line every morning since. It does not improve."
    act 1
  node thanked bramwick "Don't thank me, Fenn. I bolted that loft from the lane side for three years, hoping someone would notice. Sail."
    act 1
  node bye bramwick "Goodnight, Fenn. Don't stamp anything I'd regret."
